There are several issues here:

* what objects can monsters equip?
* what objects can a player equip when polyselfed?
* what equipped objects will stay equipped when a player polyselfs?

To take them in order:

The only monsters that can equip armour and amulets (monsters never
use rings or eyewear) are those that:

* are SMALL or larger
* are not animals
* have hands
* have brains (except for mummies and skeletons wearing their initial
    wrappings and armour).

Additionally, monsters with horns cannot wear hard helmets; body
armour and shirts can only be worn by MEDIUM humanoids, cloaks by
SMALL monsters or MEDIUM humanoids, except that hobbits can wear elven
mithril, and winged gargoyles and mariliths can't wear any of these
(wrong shape); boots can only be worn by monsters with legs, and not
by centaurs.

Only monsters with weapon attacks can wield weapons; only strong
monsters can wield two-handed weapons; silver-hating monsters will
never wield silver weapons; only monsters wearing gloves can wield
cockatrice corpses (considered as a weapon for this purpose).


So much for the NPCs. Now, you; being polyselfed into various forms
can restrict what you can equip:

You can only put on rings if you have limbs (not the same as hands,
note); you can put on amulets and eyewear without restriction (lenses
without eyes might _look_ damn stupid, but there's no law against
looking stupid).

You can only wear armour of any type if you are SMALL or larger and
have hands; you can't wear hard helmets if you have horns; body armour
and shirts can only be worn by MEDIUM humanoids, cloaks by SMALL
monsters or MEDIUM humanoids, except that hobbits can wear elven
mithril, and winged gargoyles and mariliths can't wear any of these
(wrong shape); boots can only be worn by monsters with legs, and not
by centaurs.

You can only wield weapons if you are SMALL or larger and have hands;
otherwise, no restriction (not considering two-weaponing here).


Finally, when you polyself, some equipped items are treated specially.
Armour may break or be dropped if you couldn't have worn it in that
form (dragonscale merges if you're polying to that dragon, unmerges
if it was merged and you're polying to something else, whereupon it
may break or be dropped); weapons are dropped if you couldn't have
wielded it in that form; but amulets, rings, and eyewear are _not_
removed, even if you don't have limbs to wear a ring on; in the
latter case, you can't remove it until you're in a form that does
("The ring is stuck").


(If you're thinking of asking "so, what monsters have hands? what
monsters are what size? what monsters have brains?" and so on, then
the size question is answered in mon2-343.txt. Other physical
properties _will_ be covered in mon3-343.txt when it ever gets
written, but in the meantime your best bet is either the source or Ali
Harlow's Monster Manual.)

